.TH GOCAT-SCAN 1 "December 2024" "GoCat 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gocat-scan \- port scanner
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gocat scan
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIHOST\fR \fIPORTS\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scan ports on a target host. Supports TCP and UDP scanning
with configurable concurrency and timeout.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-timeout " " \fIDURATION\fR
Port scan timeout (default: 3s)
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-concurrent " " \fICOUNT\fR
Concurrent scans (default: 100)
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-udp
Scan UDP ports
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-tcp
Scan TCP ports (default)
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-all
Scan both TCP and UDP
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format (text, json, xml)
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Verbose output
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Quiet mode (only open ports)
.SH PORT SPECIFICATION
Ports can be specified in several formats:
.TP
.B Single port
80
.TP
.B Multiple ports
80,443,8080
.TP
.B Port range
1-1000
.TP
.B Combined
22,80,443,8000-9000
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Scan single port:
.B gocat scan example.com 80
.TP
Scan port range:
.B gocat scan example.com 1-1000
.TP
Scan with timeout:
.B gocat scan --timeout 5s example.com 1-65535
.TP
JSON output:
.B gocat scan -o json example.com 1-1000
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gocat (1),
.BR nmap (1)
